1. What is a Stack?

A stack is a linear data structure in which insertion and deletion happen from one end only.

That end is called the:

TOP

Think about a stack of plates.

       ┌───────┐
TOP →  │ Plate │  ← Last inserted
       ├───────┤
       │ Plate │
       ├───────┤
       │ Plate │
       └───────┘

If you want to remove a plate, you remove the top plate first.

You cannot directly remove the bottom plate.

Therefore:

Last In → First Out

This is called:

LIFO

Last
In
First
Out

2. Basic Stack Operations

There are three extremely important operations.

1. PUSH

Adds an element to the top.

Before:

TOP
 ↓
[30]
[20]
[10]

PUSH(40)

After:

TOP
 ↓
[40]
[30]
[20]
[10]
2. POP

Removes the top element.

Before:

TOP
 ↓
[40]
[30]
[20]
[10]

POP()

After:

TOP
 ↓
[30]
[20]
[10]

The removed value is:

40

3. PEEK / TOP

Looks at the top element without removing it.

[40] ← TOP
[30]
[20]
[10]

peek() returns:

40

But 40 remains in the stack.

3. The Most Important Rule

Remember:

PUSH → INSERT
POP  → DELETE
PEEK → VIEW

And all happen at:

TOP

