Expression:

A + B * C

Because multiplication has higher precedence:

A + (B * C)
Prefix
+ A * B C
Postfix
A B C * +
15. Operator Precedence

Remember the basic order:

()
↓
*
/
%
↓
+
-

So:

A + B * C

means:

A + (B*C)

NOT:

(A+B)*C
