19. Stack and Recursion

Consider:

void fun(int n)
{
    if(n == 0)
        return;

    printf("%d ", n);
    fun(n-1);
}

Calling:

fun(3)

creates:

fun(3)
fun(2)
fun(1)
fun(0)

The calls are maintained using the call stack.

When fun(0) finishes:

fun(0) removed
fun(1) resumes
fun(1) removed
fun(2) resumes
fun(2) removed
fun(3) resumes

Again:

LIFO

